    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576-a5">

                <pb facs="0699" n="639" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg639"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Annex D.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seattle, Wash.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-24"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Collector Customs</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Victoria, British Columbia.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Replying to your favor of the 20th
                    instant, the number of skins shipped via Suez Canal to England were as follows:
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Allic I. Algar</hi>, 1,326; <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Henry Dennis</hi>, 864. The <hi rendition="#italic">Willard Ainsworth</hi>
                    also shipped 724.</p>
                <p>Skins were not examined by experts when landed at Sound ports to determine their
                    sex.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. C. Nixon.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
